<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Junaid Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1857–1938</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad Qurban Serdar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Junaid Khan was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> tribal leader of the Yomut who became the real power in the Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a> from 1918. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/young-khivans">Young Khivans</a> overthrew the khanate in 1920, he fought the Khorezm People's Soviet Republic and later Soviet rule as a leader of the Basmachi resistance, before fleeing to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, where he died.</p></div>
